From f7c645ce5e77d8d9961faa283fe598bb9931b8e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kimi <kimi@moonshot.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 01:48:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: ranging & direction-finding accuracy enhancement (v2)

- Wi-Fi FTM (802.11mc RTT) ranging: symmetric SoftAP responder +
  periodic initiator, median-filtered per-burst distances
- Bidirectional RSSI fusion via ESP-NOW protocol v2 (backward compatible)
- Channel-diversity sweep: 1/6/11 fast hopping (100ms dwell),
  per-channel first-harmonic least-squares fitting + circular-median vote
- Parabolic-interpolated peak angle + prominence gating
- BLE 5.0 Coded PHY sentinel link (NimBLE ext adv + sparse scan)
- Fusion engine with confidence levels and adaptive indoor/outdoor n
- 1m two-card calibration persisted in NVS (OK LONG on main page)
- Result page shows angle spread and confidence
- Host tests: test_radar_fusion (7 suites), extended test_radar_sweep
